    ("p", "The composite of method M against reference R in a scenario is the weighted sum of relative improvements, each clipped to [−1, 1], in aggregate throughput (0.25), Jain fairness (0.20), 5th-percentile flow throughput p5 (0.20), loss rate (0.20) and switch count (0.15). The switch count adds every radio retune, downlink and uplink (the uplink follows the parent's downlink), to the parent changes of traffic sources. It is averaged over scenarios and shown as a percentage (+0.10 is +10%). Here d = (x_M − x_R)/x_R for higher-is-better metrics, d = (x_R − x_M)/max(x_R, 0.01) for the loss rate and d = (x_R − x_M)/(x_R + 1) for the switch count. For example, against Ko in S2: throughput 66.87 vs. 55.42 Mb/s (d = 20.7%), Jain +4.6%, p5 +21.4%, loss rate 0.240 vs. 0.374 (d = 35.8%) and switches 44.3 vs. 771.4 (d = 94.1%), which weight to a composite of +31.7%. The pre-registered criteria are (1) ≥ +10% against every method on A+B, (2) significant (Holm) in ≥ 60% of scenarios, (3) no scenario worse than Ko by more than 5%, and (4) criterion 1 still holds when any weight changes by ±50%. The 95% confidence interval is a t-interval over the matrix of composites for every pair of training seeds, so it includes the training variance of both methods."),
    ("p", "Hysteresis, the margin-selection rule and this confidence interval were added after the first test evaluation, and the airtime model was calibrated after the ns-3 results were seen; all of these changes are recorded with dates. Every learned method was retrained after calibration, and the margin is chosen only on validation. The earlier model had a per-node GRU and tied with Yuan+H, and the ablation on the test set found the model without GRU better (Section 6.4). Because this was found after seeing the test set, we wrote a protocol before running that fixed the model, five seeds, the same margin rule, new topologies 40–59 never used before, and the criteria (P1) beat Yuan+H by at least +5% with a lower bound above 0, (P2) lower bound above 0 against every other baseline, and (P3) all four criteria pass. The protocol file was created before the run but committed to git only after it, so its timing rests on file and run-log timestamps. All of them passed (m = 2 again), so Section 6 reports the model without GRU, and topologies 40–59 are the main reference set."),
